{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1073","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Berland Fair"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"XXI Berland Annual Fair is coming really soon! Traditionally fair consists of $$$n$$$ booths, arranged in a circle. The booths are numbered $$$1$$$ through $$$n$$$ clockwise with $$$n$$$ being adjacent to $$$1$$$. The $$$i$$$-th booths sells some candies for the price of $$$a_i$$$ burles per item. Each booth has an unlimited supply of candies."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarp has decided to spend at most $$$T$$$ burles at the fair. However, he has some plan in mind for his path across the booths:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" at first, he visits booth number $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if he has enough burles to buy "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" candy from the current booth, then he buys it immediately; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" then he proceeds to the next booth in the clockwise order (regardless of if he bought a candy or not). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarp's money is finite, thus the process will end once he can no longer buy candy at any booth."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Calculate the number of candies Polycarp will buy."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le T \\le 10^{18}$$$) — the number of booths at the fair and the initial amount of burles Polycarp has."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the price of the single candy at booth number $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the total number of candies Polycarp will buy."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 38\n5 2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 21\n2 4 100 2 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the first example. Here are Polycarp's moves until he runs out of money:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$1$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 33$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$2$$$, buys candy for $$$2$$$, $$$T = 31$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$3$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 26$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$1$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 21$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$2$$$, buys candy for $$$2$$$, $$$T = 19$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$3$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 14$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$1$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 9$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$2$$$, buys candy for $$$2$$$, $$$T = 7$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$3$$$, buys candy for $$$5$$$, $$$T = 2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$1$$$, buys no candy, not enough money; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Booth $$$2$$$, buys candy for $$$2$$$, $$$T = 0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No candy can be bought later. The total number of candies bought is $$$10$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example he has $$$1$$$ burle left at the end of his path, no candy can be bought with this amount."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1073D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1073/problem/D"}